{"run_id":"run_442f5e0d2f3a","schema_version":"0.1","seq":11,"t_ms":11,"text":"The **Diligence Material Handling Standard** is short. Its main rules:\n\n1. **Material is compartmented.** All diligence material is kept within set compartments, not shared openly.\n2. **Each item lists its named reviewers.** The people allowed to review it are recorded on every document or artifact.\n3. **Sharing outside that list needs approval.** Anyone not named on the artifact can only receive it if the workstream owner approves.\n4. **The standard covers process only.** It contains no diligence content itself.\n\nIt doesn't say how approvals are recorded, who counts as a workstream owner, or what happens if material is shared without approval. The Project Halyard workstream index may say who owns each workstream. I can check it if that would help.","turn":3,"type":"agent.message"}
